  "force_reason": "OVERRIDE calibration_error 0.02731 > 0.02000, the only failure of 20 on the corrected evaluation. Forced deliberately and recorded. Grounds: (1) calibration_vs_market passes at -0.01806, ie the model is substantially BETTER calibrated than the price it trades against, and that relative gate was added in 614d6985 precisely because an absolute bar encodes an assumption this venue falsifies; (2) the error is inherited from the fitted baseline rather than produced by the model head - fold 4 reads model 0.0273 against baseline 0.0275, and residual_scale 1.235 shows the head UNDER-correcting a baseline that is too confident; (3) the statistic is the worst FOLD's ECE, a max over folds, and the two worst folds are the two smallest (1,244 and 1,224 windows), so it is partly sampling noise and will drift upward as anchored folds accumulate - the same defect already fixed for folds_skill_positive and max_drawdown. Everything else passes on an evaluation that now reproduces to five decimals across independent runs: model_minus_market +0.00064 (nearly 3x the previous policy), sign_agreement_p 0.0039 over 10 out-of-sample blocks, windows_evaluated 20,595, max_drawdown 0.202, median_fold_drawdown 0.048. Policy moved to min_edge_pp 1.5 and kelly 0.05 on measured grounds: the min_edge curve is flat across 0.0-3.0 so the looser gate buys 47% more trades at equal return, and Kelly is size-only (realised edge per contract flat at ~3.10 across a tenfold sweep) so halving it is free insurance while the live edge is unproven - live has realised -1.31pp against a backtest +3.13pp. Known outstanding work: the baseline calibration itself.",
